# SATYA NETRA — Real-Time Multimodal Deepfake Detection Platform

**SIH 2026 | Problem Statement USICT028 | Category: AI Safety & Media Verification**

SATYA NETRA is a real-time deepfake detection platform for live video streams.
It combines **multiple deep-learning models** through a custom multimodal
fusion engine with temporal aggregation and streak-based alerting.

## What's inside

- **Three pre-trained detectors** — Vision Transformer (ViT), EfficientNet
  (secondary visual detector), and a Wav2Vec2-derived audio classifier
- **Custom-trained LSTM temporal classifier** — trained in-house on
  FaceForensics++ using ViT-derived frame embeddings (val AUC 0.80, F1 0.77)
- **Custom multimodal fusion engine** — combines all four signals with
  configurable weights and graceful degradation when signals are missing
- **Temporal aggregation** — rolling window + streak-based alert logic
- **Live capture + video-file modes** — webcam with mic (with VU meter)
  and uploaded videos with real-time or full-analysis playback
- **Streamlit dashboard** — per-signal confidence, fused score, latency, FPS,
  alert log

## Architecture
Live Video / Uploaded File
↓
Frame Extraction + Audio Extraction (or live mic)
↓
Face Detection (Haar Cascade)
↓
┌────────┬────────┬────────┬────────┐
↓ ↓ ↓ ↓ ↓
ViT EfficientNet Audio Temporal-LSTM (custom-trained)
└────────┴────────┴────────┴────────┘
↓
Multimodal Fusion Engine
↓
Temporal Aggregator (rolling window + streak)
↓
Live Dashboard + Alert Log

## Setup

### Prerequisites
- Python 3.13
- Windows / Mac / Linux
- Optional: NVIDIA GPU for faster inference

### Install

```bash
cd backend
python -m venv venv
venv\Scripts\activate       # Windows PowerShell
# source venv/bin/activate  # Mac/Linux

pip install -r requirements.txt
```

*(If PowerShell blocks the activate script, run
`Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope CurrentUser -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned` first.)*

### Run

```bash
streamlit run app.py
```

App opens at `http://localhost:8501`. First run downloads pre-trained models
(~500 MB total, one-time).

## Project structure
backend/
├── app.py # Streamlit UI layer
├── config.py # All tunable parameters
├── requirements.txt
├── detectors/
│ ├── face.py # Face detection (Haar Cascade)
│ ├── video.py # Visual deepfake models (ViT + EfficientNet)
│ ├── audio.py # Audio deepfake model
│ └── temporal.py # LSTM temporal classifier (loads trained .pt)
├── pipeline/
│ ├── aggregator.py # Rolling window + streak-based alerts
│ └── fusion.py # Multimodal fusion algorithm
├── inputs/
│ ├── webcam.py # Live webcam capture
│ ├── microphone.py # Live mic capture with ring buffer + VU meter
│ ├── audio_extract.py # Extract audio from uploaded video (ffmpeg)
│ ├── video_file.py # Uploaded video file processing
│ └── webrtc.py # WebRTC stub (Phase 3)
└── training/ # LSTM training pipeline (see training/README.md)
├── lstm_model.py # LSTM architecture
├── ff_dataset.py # FaceForensics++ dataset loader
├── extract_faces.py # Video → face crops
├── generate_embeddings.py# Face crops → ViT embeddings
├── train_lstm.py # Training loop
└── models/
└── lstm_temporal.pt # Trained model weights


## Configuration (edit `config.py`)

| Setting | Default | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `WINDOW_SIZE` | 5 | Rolling window for score smoothing |
| `ALERT_THRESHOLD` | 0.6 | Smoothed score above this = alert territory |
| `CONSECUTIVE_ALERTS_NEEDED` | 3 | Consecutive over-threshold before alert fires |
| `FRAME_SKIP` | 10 | Run model every Nth frame (set to 1 on GPU) |
| `FUSION_WEIGHT_VIDEO_PRIMARY` | 0.35 | ViT weight |
| `FUSION_WEIGHT_VIDEO_SECONDARY` | 0.25 | EfficientNet weight |
| `FUSION_WEIGHT_AUDIO` | 0.15 | Audio detector weight |
| `FUSION_WEIGHT_TEMPORAL` | 0.25 | LSTM temporal weight |

## LSTM training

See `training/README.md` for full details on training the temporal LSTM
on FaceForensics++.

Current trained model metrics (`training/models/lstm_metrics.json`):

- Accuracy    : 73%
- Precision   : 69%
- Recall      : 86%
- F1 Score    : 0.77
- ROC-AUC     : 0.80

Trained on 1000 real + 1000 fake videos from FaceForensics++ (c23,
Deepfakes / Face2Face / FaceSwap / NeuralTextures methods).

## GPU migration

When moving to a CUDA-capable GPU:

```bash
pip uninstall torch torchvision -y
pip install torch==2.5.1 torchvision==0.20.1 --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121
```

Then in `config.py` set `FRAME_SKIP = 1` and increase `WEBCAM_WIDTH/HEIGHT`
to `1280x720`. Model auto-detects GPU — no other code changes needed.

## Known limitations

- CPU inference is slow (~500-800 ms/frame per visual model). Real-time
  performance requires GPU.
- Haar Cascade face detector struggles with side profiles and occlusion.
  MediaPipe or MTCNN is planned for improvement.
- Live audio deepfake detection requires a microphone; uploaded videos
  without an audio track fall back to video-only fusion.

## Team

**Team SPARTAN** — SIH 2026, USICT028


